TS doesn't narrow `match` after `await failPhase(...)` because failPhase returns Promise<never> — the await of a never promise should narrow... but TS's control flow analysis treats the awaited call as potentially completing (it doesn't track Promise<never> for narrowing reliably in all cases). Simple fix: restructure to early-return pattern with match null check first:

```ts
const match = /(\d+)\.(\d+)/.exec(versionText);
if (version.exitCode !== 0 || match === null) {
  await failPhase(...); // throws
  return; // unreachable, but silences narrowing
}
```

Hmm — actually the cleanest: `if (match === null) { await failPhase(...) }` then TS narrows match after the if-block only if failPhase's return type makes the block never-complete... it doesn't with await. Add explicit `return` after failPhase calls? failPhase is Promise<never> so the `return` after is dead code but satisfies TS. Hmm — actually with a `return` statement, the code after the if-block only executes when the condition was false → match non-null → narrowed. Let me just restructure:

```ts
if (version.exitCode !== 0 || match === null) {
  await failPhase(ctx, "prerequisites", ...);
  return; // unreachable — failPhase throws
}
```

That works for narrowing. Let me apply this pattern where needed (only here since other failPhase uses don't need narrowing after).

