Analyzing the 6 failures:

1. **"re-run skips install/build/start"** — need detail. Probably: prerequisites' demoServerAlreadyUp works, but... the re-run test seeds `world.serverUp = true` + state file. Ports probe: portAnswers true for 8080/4173 when serverUp — prerequisites: demoServerAlreadyUp checks state + fetchText health → OK → skip. install: probe node_modules/.bin — seeded in dirs → skip. build: artifacts seeded → skip. start: already → skip. env+smoke run. Then the state assertions... Need the actual failure detail — it was truncated. Let me look closer at what failed. Possibly the server pid carryover? The state's server has apiPort 8080 matching config → carried over. Hmm.

2. **"smoke failure tears down"** — `world.started.length` expected 1 but the stop() REMOVES the handle from world.started (`world.started = world.started.filter(...)`)! So after teardown, length = 0. My test then checks length 1 — wrong. Fix the test: capture the handle BEFORE... the handle is removed from the array, so I should check `handle.stopped === true` differently. Let me change stop() to NOT remove from started (keep it, just mark stopped) — or the test holds a reference. Simplest: in the test, grab `world.started[0]` BEFORE... but teardown happens during the run. Alternative: don't remove in stop(); keep array as the record of everything started; assert via the "stopped" getter. Change the fake: stop() sets stopped=true + serverUp=false (no array mutation). Then `world.started.length === 1` + `world.started[0].stopped === true`.

3. **"health-wait timeout"** — `world.started[0]` undefined because stop() removed it. Same fix.

